cent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"In a PostgreSQL database I have two views, where one is a plain view and the other is a materialized view:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n>>> inspector.get_view_names(schema=self.schema)\r\n['my_plain_view', 'my_materialized_view']\r\n```\r\n\r\nbut if I call inspection with a specific view type, then the `get_view_names()` is cached too aggressively by the `@reflection.cache` decorator in the `PGDialect.get_view_names()` method:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n>>> inspector.get_view_names(schema=self.schema, include=('plain',))\r\n['my_plain_view']\r\n>>> inspector.get_view_names(schema=self.schema, include=('materialized',))\r\n['my_plain_view']\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is because the `include` argument is not considered in the `PGInspector.info_cache` entry.\r\n\r\nListing materialized views works fine when there is no cache:\r\n```python\r\n>>> inspector.get_view_names(schema=self.schema, include=('materialized',))\r\n['my_materialized_view']\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is with Python 3.7.4 and SQLAlchemy 1.3.8 on Ubuntu 16.04.","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{